{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"ea1c17fd09ece594a5caa866b40ddaa8b1e40ba80a2e5624d57a2bd5d2cee4f1","packTokens":5536,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":5259,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nState, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot web app shall provide email-and-password sign-in for administrator-managed accounts without self-service registration or SSO, allow Administrators to manage accounts and assign Administrator or Operator roles, and show role-appropriate controls and pages.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An administrator-managed account exists and the sign-in page is open when The user inspects the sign-in controls and submits the account credentials then The screen shows email and password fields, no self-service registration or SSO controls, and the signed-in user's role and available pages\",\n    \"Given An Administrator is signed in when The Administrator opens user management and the main navigation then The screen shows account controls with email, password, and Administrator and Operator role values, plus user, import, configuration, plan, feeding, weight, dashboard, and report controls\",\n    \"Given An Operator is signed in when The Operator opens the main navigation and user-management page then The screen shows plan, feeding, weight, dashboard, and report controls and does not show user-management, import, or configuration controls\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an Administrator starts synchronization, the Feedlot web app shall request procurement and receiving records from the configured mock source and display returned records, source identifiers, per-record synchronization outcomes, and errors.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The mock source contains PO and receiving records with vendor, cost, head count, weight, breed, age, and source fields when An Administrator starts synchronization then The request targets the configured mock source and the screen shows the returned record fields and synchronization status for each record\",\n    \"Given A source record has a previously imported source record ID and another source record has failed synchronization when An Administrator starts another synchronization then The screen shows the returned update outcome for the previously imported ID and the failed record's ID and error, without showing the failed record as a successful import\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot web app shall display PO-line-to-lot-to-pen traceability, available procurement and animal fields, pen capacity and current animal counts, and lot purchase-cost allocations proportional to assigned received head counts.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API provides a PO line mapped to multiple lots and pens, with available procurement and animal fields when A user opens the imported record details or procurement traceability view then The screen shows the PO line, source identifiers, related lots and pens, available vendor, cost, head-count, weight, breed, age, and source fields, and each pen's capacity and current animal count\",\n    \"Given A PO line has a total cost of 1000 USD and two lots assigned 60 and 40 received animals when A user opens the PO line's lot allocations then The screen shows purchase-cost allocation values of 600 USD and 400 USD for the respective lots\",\n    \"Given The source response omits an animal's sex when A user opens that animal's imported details then The screen shows the sex field as Unknown\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens a lot lifecycle view, the Feedlot web app shall display target weight, lifecycle milestones, projected market date, and the growth assumption used, using measured ADG when available and otherwise the configured yard expected daily gain.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API provides a lot target weight, receiving date, and measured ADG when A user opens that lot's lifecycle view then The screen shows the target weight, lifecycle milestones, measured ADG as the projection assumption, and projected market date\",\n    \"Given The API provides no usable measured ADG and provides the yard expected daily gain and any lot-specific target override when A user opens that lot's lifecycle view then The screen shows the projected market date, target weight used, and configured yard expected daily gain as the projection assumption\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot web app shall allow users to view and enter feed inventory item fields, retain entered units for display, show normalized calculation values where applicable, and display opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API provides an inventory item with stock values, entered units, cost, nutrition fields, and storage location when A user opens the feed inventory item then The screen shows the item name, category, available quantity, entered unit, cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values\",\n    \"Given An inventory item is entered in tons with a cost per ton when A user opens its cost details then The screen shows the entered units and normalized calculation values in pounds and USD per pound\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens inventory projections, the Feedlot web app shall display estimates for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month, and annual horizons using the configured wastage ratio in estimates and projections, without displaying a separate wastage stock movement.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Inventory, projected consumption, and a configured wastage ratio are available when A user opens inventory projections then The screen shows estimates for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month, and annual horizons and the wastage ratio used\",\n    \"Given The inventory movement response contains receipts and feed consumption when A user reviews the movement list and forecast then The screen shows the returned stock movements and no separate wastage movement\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot web app shall allow users to create and view rations with ingredient proportions, nutritional values, intended animal or weight range, and calculated cost per pound using normalized calculation units while retaining entered units for display.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user enters a ration name, type, ingredients, proportions, and intended animal type or weight range when The user saves and opens the ration then The screen shows the returned ration's ingredients, proportions, dry-matter percentage, energy value, intended range, and calculated cost per pound in USD\",\n    \"Given A ration's ingredients have costs entered in different supported weight units when The user opens the ration cost details then The screen shows the calculated cost in USD per pound and retains the entered units for display\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user submits nutrition or animal-range constraints for ration optimization, the Feedlot web app shall display candidate ingredient mixes with costs and trade-offs and require an explicit save or assign action before a candidate is saved, assigned, or used.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user has entered nutrition or animal-range constraints and candidate mixes are returned when The user requests and views candidate mixes then The screen shows each candidate's ingredient proportions, cost, and trade-offs without marking it saved or assigned\",\n    \"Given An optimization candidate is displayed when The user selects save or assign and that action is accepted then The screen shows the returned candidate as saved or assigned only after the action is accepted\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user generates a dated pen feeding plan, the Feedlot web app shall display planned quantity as the bunk rate in pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day multiplied by planned animal count, with plan details and separate lot allocations proportional to current lot animal counts in the pen.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A pen plan uses a bunk rate of 25 pounds per animal per day and a planned animal count of 40 when A user generates the plan then The screen shows a planned feed quantity of 1000 pounds and the plan date, pen, ration, feeding time, cost, expected energy, and status\",\n    \"Given A pen plan is for 1000 pounds and its current animals are split 60 to one lot and 40 to another when A user opens the plan's lot allocations then The screen shows separate planned-feed allocations of 600 and 400 pounds for the respective lots\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens pen feeding schedules, the Feedlot web app shall show plans by delivery date and pen with planned quantity and Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Pen plans exist with delivery dates and statuses when A user opens feeding schedules then The screen shows each plan's date, pen, ration, planned quantity, and Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped status\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an Operator records a feeding activity, the Feedlot web app shall allow an activity with or without a matching plan, submit the activity details and lot allocations, and display the returned planned and actual quantities, variance when linked to a plan, inventory result, feed cost, energy, feeding status, lot allocations, and lot rollups.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A linked plan is for 900 pounds and an accepted activity records 950 pounds delivered when The Operator opens the activity details then The screen shows planned feed of 900 pounds, actual feed of 950 pounds, and a variance of 50 pounds, along with the activity fields\",\n    \"Given A pen contains animals from multiple lots and the API returns lot allocations for an activity when The Operator views the saved activity then The request contains separate lot allocations and the screen shows the returned delivered-feed allocations and corresponding lot consumption and cost rollups\",\n    \"Given No matching plan exists for the activity date and the save response is successful when The Operator saves and views the feeding activity then The screen shows the activity as unplanned, the returned activity, and lot totals\",\n    \"Given An activity does not match the available plan date, pen, or lot when The activity is displayed in a list or detail view then The screen shows a plan-mismatch indicator\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a feeding activity is accepted, the Feedlot web app shall display the inventory consumption and lot allocations returned by the API; it shall not assert a web-side inventory decrement formula.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API response for an accepted activity contains ingredient consumption and multiple lot allocations when The activity and affected inventory or lot summaries are displayed then The screen shows the returned ingredient quantities, as-fed lot quantities, feed costs, and separate lot allocations\",\n    \"Given An accepted activity returns inventory results that include a wastage-based decrement when The Operator views the saved activity and affected inventory then The screen shows the returned inventory result without replacing it with a web-calculated value\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a feeding save is refused for insufficient stock, the Feedlot web app shall retain entered activity values and display the returned error without presenting the activity as saved or displaying updated inventory or lot totals.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An Operator enters a feeding activity and the feed service refuses it for insufficient stock, returning unchanged totals when The Operator saves the activity then The screen retains the entered values, shows the returned error, does not show the activity as saved, and continues to show the prior inventory and lot totals\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized user edits or cancels a saved feeding activity, the Feedlot web app shall display the returned activity state, inventory totals, and lot totals, or display the returned error if the API refuses the change.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API accepts an edit or cancellation and returns updated totals when The user views the activity and affected summaries then The screen shows the returned corrected or canceled activity and recalculated inventory and lot total values\",\n    \"Given The API refuses an edit or cancellation when An authorized user views the action result then The screen shows the returned error message and existing activity details\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an Operator records a lot weight measurement, the Feedlot web app shall submit the dated measurement fields and display the returned measurement in the lot's dated weight history and trend.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An Operator enters a measurement with date, number of animals weighed, average weight, total lot weight, gain since the prior measurement, and notes when The Operator saves and opens the lot's weight history then The screen shows the returned measurement fields in the lot's dated weight history and trend\",\n    \"Given The API accepts a correction to a saved weight measurement and returns updated values when An authorized user opens the lot history and metrics then The screen shows the corrected record and returned recalculated metrics and weight trend\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens lot performance, the Feedlot web app shall display returned days on feed, total weight gain, ADG, total as-fed feed consumed, FCR, feed cost of gain, and projected ship date, and refresh those values after an accepted feeding or weight event.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API supplies lot metrics for a lot with receiving date, entry and current average weights, feeding events, and target weight when A user opens the lot performance view then The screen shows days on feed, total weight gain, ADG, total as-fed feed consumed, FCR using as-fed pounds, feed cost of gain, and projected ship date\",\n    \"Given A feeding or weight event has been accepted and the API supplies refreshed lot metrics when A user views the lot performance screen after the event then The screen shows the refreshed metric values returned for that lot\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens lot financial performance and insights, the Feedlot web app shall display feed cost of gain separately, available purchase and feed costs and recorded sale revenue, label broader ROI unavailable when required data is missing, and display returned feeding or sale-timing recommendations.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A lot has purchase and feed costs but no sale proceeds or complete relevant costs when A user opens lot profitability then The screen shows available purchase and feed cost components, feed cost of gain, and a broader ROI unavailable label\",\n    \"Given The API supplies recorded sale proceeds, required costs, and recommendations based on feeding and weight trends when A user opens lot financial performance and insights then The screen shows recorded sale revenue, returned broader profitability values, and returned feeding-adjustment or sale-timing recommendations\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens the operations dashboard, the Feedlot web app shall display active lots and pens, operational counts and inventory, ration and plan information, feed and weight performance, energy use, and lot rankings.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API supplies dashboard data for lots, pens, inventory, rations, plans, activities, and weights when A user opens the operations dashboard then The screen shows active lots and pens based on current animal counts above zero, animal counts per lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily pen bunk rates, planned versus actual feed, total feed and cost, starting and current weights, weight gain, ADG, FCR, cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens the yard summary, the Feedlot web app shall display aggregate metrics across active lots, including total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API supplies aggregate values for active lots when A user opens the yard summary then The screen shows total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens the dedicated Feed-to-Gain report, the Feedlot web app shall display lot comparisons for ADG, FCR, and cost of gain and provide date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters, with sex filtering limited to known values.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The report has lot data including known and unknown sex values when A user opens the report and applies date-range, breed, sex, or pen filters then The screen shows matching lots with ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, and the sex filter offers known values only\",\n    \"Given A user selects report filters when The report results refresh then The screen shows only rows matching the selected date range, breed, known sex, and pen values\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user exports the Feed-to-Gain report, the Feedlot web app shall provide the displayed or filtered report data as a CSV or PDF file.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user has a Feed-to-Gain report displayed with or without filters when The user selects CSV or PDF export then The browser download list contains a file in the selected format with the displayed report data\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens the demo and presentation view, the Feedlot web app shall show mock operational data and materials covering the proposed solution and architecture diagrams, demo flow, coding prompts, validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Mock demo data and presentation content are available when A user opens or reviews the demo and presentation view then The screen shows sample operational data and sections for the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, demo flow, coding super prompt and other prompts, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"Every page shall use a responsive web layout for phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n  \"The main application flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.\",\n  \"The web app shall support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n  \"The user interface shall use English text and left-to-right layout.\",\n  \"The web app shall have staging and production deployment targets built through a pipeline.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}